tools.read_mathlib({path:"Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/ContDiff/FTaylorSeries.lean",start_line:792,line_count:71})
]);rs.forEach((r,i)=>text({i,result:r}));

const qs=[
"^theorem tendsto_integral_of_dominated_convergence |^theorem integral_prod |^theorem integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt |^theorem exists_hasDerivAt_eq_slope ",
"^noncomputable def fderiv|^def fderiv|^noncomputable irreducible_def fderiv|^def volume.*Measure|volume_pi",
"^def HasCompactSupport|^def support |^def HasFiniteIntegral"];
const rs=await Promise.allSettled(qs.map(query=>tools.search_mathlib({query})));rs.forEach((r,i)=>text({query:qs[i],result:r}));
text(await tools.read_mathlib({path:"Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/Deriv/Basic.lean",start_line:112,line_count:55}));

const loc=(document,pointer)=>({document,pointer});
const artifact={
checks:{
source_route_and_coverage:{
verdict:"PASS",
notes:"Read all nine frozen inputs and minimal-translation.md, audit-b.md and lean-writing.md. There are no external E roots. Compared the canonical spec and all five NL0 inferences, including every argument paragraph, output and direct input boundary. All 18 paragraphs are preserved: S001–S003 map to T001 (N001); S004–S008 to T002/T003 (N002); S009–S013 to T004/T005/T006 (N003); S014–S016 to T007/T008 (N004); S017–S018 to T009/T010 (P). The route remains differentiated unit constraint, common compact support and integrability, mean-value domination followed by sequential dominated convergence, coordinate FTC followed by Fubini, then cancellation and mean-value constancy. In particular T008 explicitly requires coordinate/product-measure transport, endpoint vanishing, closed-interval derivative existence and interval integrability, and the n=1 measure-one remaining factor. It does not replace the accepted argument with a new integration-by-parts theorem or impose a new project hypothesis. The background supplement and copied source paragraphs match the frozen source-map material.",
locations:[loc("spec.json","/full_target"),loc("nl0.json","/inferences"),loc("nl0.json","/propositions"),loc("source-map.json","/paragraph_mapping"),loc("contract.json","/source_steps"),loc("plan.json","/steps"),loc("plan.json","/terminal")]
},
parameters_and_allowed_inputs:{
verdict:"PASS",
notes:"Compared the complete P signature in type-Check.lean with spec H001–H006 and the contract binders. n,m:ℕ with 1≤n∧1≤m retain both positive integer dimensions; u has real Euclidean spatial and target coordinates, and q is one fixed unit vector. H002 demands joint smoothness only on 0<t. H004 and H005 have the original spatial and positive-time quantifiers; H005 is pointwise ∃a:ℝ for utt−Σj uxxj=a•u, without a selected smooth scalar or the derived explicit PDE as input. H006 quantifies each real 0<s<t, chooses one compact C for the entire closed interval, and asserts equality with that same q outside C. H003 is retained in P although unused locally. The final domain is nonvacuous: for positive dimensions a constant unit map satisfies all hypotheses. Through implementation helpers the direct frontiers are R001: H002,H004,H005; R002: H001,H002,H006; R003: H002,N002; R004: H001,H002,N002; R005: H002,N001,N002,N003,N004, with Mathlib freely available. There are no additional external assumptions, object fields, scalar-field changes or hidden target-bearing construction fields.",
locations:[loc("spec.json","/parameters"),loc("spec.json","/hypotheses"),loc("nl0.json","/inferences"),loc("contract.json","/parameters"),loc("contract.json","/premises"),loc("contract.json","/objects"),loc("contract.json","/shared_obligations"),loc("plan.json","/steps")]
},
representations_and_conversion_obligations:{
verdict:"PASS",
notes:"Independently verified the P correspondence explanation against the definitions and pinned library. PiL2.lean defines EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) as PiLp 2 and its inner product as the finite coordinate sum; PiLp.single 2 j 1 has value 1 at j and 0 elsewhere. Thus Fin n bijectively labels 1,…,n, spatial is the actual coordinate differential, laplace is the componentwise coordinate sum, and density is the Frobenius sum of squared coordinate derivatives with no factor 1/2. The ContDiff scope defines ∞ in ℕ∞ω as the embedded ℕ∞ top, below ω; it means all finite smoothness orders, not analyticity. Restriction of the total u gives a source map, and arbitrary extension of any source map to t≤0 gives the converse: the positive-time domain is open, so all derivatives and energy germs used here are local to the restriction. No smooth extension across zero is required. The pinned Euclidean volume transport identifies volume with product coordinate Lebesgue measure, including Dirac mass one in dimension zero. T003 retains positive box radius, ofReal((2R)^n), and finite mass. Integrable means AEStronglyMeasurable plus HasFiniteIntegral; its explicit assertion prevents the total integral from weakening the endpoint. Positive-order iteratedFDeriv encodes all coordinate mixed derivatives in both directions by evaluation and multilinearity under smoothness. T004 explicitly assigns mixed-derivative identification and derivative existence; T008 assigns the actual representation/measure conversion before FTC/Fubini. HasDerivAt energy 0 is equivalent to differentiability and derivative zero on this open time interval, in both directions.",
locations:[loc("spec.json","/definitions"),loc("spec.json","/conclusion"),loc("nl0.json","/propositions/11"),loc("contract.json","/header"),loc("contract.json","/representation"),loc("contract.json","/endpoint_correspondence/P"),loc("contract.json","/conclusion"),loc("plan.json","/steps/3"),loc("plan.json","/steps/7")]
},
statements_and_local_plans:{
verdict:"PASS",
notes:"Compared every complete T001–T010 signature, including parameter, premise and instance binders, with the plan and source. T001 retains every N001 identity, including the value of every scalar satisfying normality. T003 retains every N002 clause with joint C,R,η,B witnesses, all seven term-list entries, global positive-time smoothness, positive-order derivative vanishing and the simultaneous closed-window bound. Its coordinate-indexed list is nonvacuous at the source boundary because H001 supplies n≥1. Helpers without H001 do not introduce an inconsistency: outside the box T003 gives local equality with q directly, and for n=0 the spatial space is the measure-one singleton; T006 also has H002. T004/T006 retain the actual density derivative, exact factor 2 formula, energy derivative and integrability of each summand in N003. T007/T008 retain the product rule, compact support, both N004 integrability claims and the signed identity. T005 handles both signs of nonzero increments; T006 retains the source sequential limit argument. The pinned dominated-convergence premises include norm domination, integrable bound and almost-everywhere strong measurability, all assigned in T005/T006. T008 assigns endpoint derivatives and interval integrability for FTC and product integrability for Fubini. T009 performs the source cancellation; T010 exports all of P, including constancy for every pair of positive times. The acyclic dependency graph discharges every internal input from earlier assigned obligations; no internal result remains an external H. Header definitions are constructions, not assumptions of the target. type-result.json reports successful strict declaration elaboration only; these judgments establish semantic interface/plan fidelity, not completed local proofs or assembly closure.",
locations:[loc("nl0.json","/propositions"),loc("nl0.json","/inferences"),loc("spec.json","/conclusion"),loc("contract.json","/header"),loc("contract.json","/conclusion"),loc("plan.json","/steps"),loc("plan.json","/terminal"),loc("type-result.json","/status")]
